<title>USA: Clinton to pursue trade in Asia, Latam, Rubin says.</title>
<headline>Clinton to pursue trade in Asia, Latam, Rubin says.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin said on Friday President Clinton will continue to pursue an active trade agenda during his second term in office.</p>
<p>&quot;In the second term, we will work to continue trade liberalization in Latin America and Asia particularly,&quot; Rubin said in a speech to the Bretton Woods Committee annual meeting.</p>
<p>He cautioned, however, that securing renewal from Congress of fast-track negotiating authority will be key to the efforts.</p>
</text>
